  "reason": "Evidence: Our best configuration (config_002, acc=0.635) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, and all five completed experiments use PCA. We have no data on whether a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200) could improve performance, which is a major unexplored design axis. Question: config_036 is identical to config_002 in every parameter except RNA encoder (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000), with all other settings held at their empirically best values (multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted). This isolates the effect of the RNA representation. Why best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against our current best, directly testing whether nonlinear learned embeddings capture biological signal that PCA misses. If scvi_n200 improves accuracy, it opens a promising exploitation direction; if not, we confirm PCA sufficiency and can redirect budget toward the image encoder or other axes with higher expected information gain."
}

